1:\section{Open Questions and Research Agenda}
3:\subsection{Measurement Gaps}
5:Anthropic 公开提出 several open gaps:
7:\begin{itemize}
8:    \item How to quantify ``alignment drift'' in the wild?
9:    \item How to estimate human override fatigue when multiple Agent versions run concurrently?
10:    \item How to instrument slow-moving capabilities (e.g., strategic reasoning) before they surface in benchmarks?
11:\end{itemize}
13:\begin{knowledgebox}{Action Items}
14:Every new capability launch must include (1) measurement plan, (2) failure signature sheet, (3) human-in-the-loop trigger.
15:\end{knowledgebox}
17:\subsection{Research Directions}
19:Ben Mann highlights:
21:\begin{itemize}
22:    \item ``Capability contour'' research—mapping the Pareto frontier of autonomy vs. controllability
23:    \item Multimodal evaluation—ensuring Agent maintains alignment when tool outputs are visual/audio
24:    \item Policy orchestration—how to mix synchronous/asynchronous Agent families safely
25:\end{itemize}
27:\subsection{本章小结}
29:现阶段最大的研究挑战是让 measurement/safety/governance 三条线同时向前推进：需要更细的 alignment metrics、multi-agent orchestration studies、以及验证治理 artifact 的实际效能。

